# K1: the first attach of the speed image on the AUDITED gate profile with the new flag on (c2-packed-tp4-gate carries
# QWEN_FAST_TP_KV_SLIDE=1 and every audit): an all-four reset, then a smoke of a warmup, the lifecycle warm (one short answer at
# each prefill size, twice: cold then warm TTFT), one coding stream and four concurrent streams (two short prompts in the ramp, two
# long ones at the steady state: the v140 mix). This is the cheap attach that runs the slide kernel over two KV heads on a card for
# the first time (no earlier run: the pair ran it at four heads, and the S2 window's one-card jobs were K64j and GDN). The audits stay on so a verify or collective
# fault is caught here, not in a timed arm. NOT a timed arm (the audits cost about 31 ms of readback per round).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card speed window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/speed and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image K0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; the first engine build 10-30 min (kernel compile on a cold cache; the slide adds one kernel);
# the four tests 8-15 min: 20 / 35 / 90 min (a collective hang runs the 80-min ready loop, then the reset).
# Read: the ready line; the launched-argv line (profile c2-packed-tp4-gate, QWEN_FAST_TP=4, QWEN_FAST_TP_KV_SLIDE=1); the
# "[PINDIAG] eager publication warmed" line (the attach warm publishes through the slide at history_rows 2048, so the slide kernel is
# built at attach); no attach refusal; the verify t1 audit lines with no audit mismatch; the warm_lifecycle cold against warm TTFT
# per size; coherent text in coding and concurrent4; the [PACKED-PHASE] and [PACKED-PUBLISH] lines (kv_history.prepare in the ramp
# users' commits: expect single-digit ms, not the ~310 ms of v140).
# STOP on an attach refusal, a hang, an audit mismatch, garbage text, or a ramp commit still above 50 ms: the smoke step now
# ENFORCES the last three and an errored stream (scripts/ci/c2_smoke_check.py exits non-zero), so the chain stops by itself.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-speed-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-gate
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,warm_lifecycle,coding,concurrent4
